Provenance
==========

This project began as a fork of dsh-context
(https://github.com/bowenliang123/dsh-context), Copyright the dsh-context
contributors, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The upstream
licence text is kept unmodified in LICENSE.apache, and upstream's own documents
are kept for provenance in .upstream-README.md and .upstream-AGENTS.md.

Since then the plugin has been **rewritten from scratch**: the module layout,
the decomposition and every implementation are new. Upstream served as a
behavioural reference (what the surfaces must show, which log events exist, how
the harness seam is used), not as code to carry over. No source file from the
earlier fork remains in src/.

What the rewrite preserves, deliberately, because these are contracts other
software and existing user data depend on:

  * the package name `dsh-cost-breakdown`, the loader row id `cost-breakdown`
    (which is also the host settings namespace), and the locale namespace;
  * the package entry shape: `main` -> lib/index.js (host, ESM), the
    `./client` / `./package.json` / `./locale/*.json` export entries, and the
    `window.__ModuleLoader__.load({ id, factory })` handoff for the browser half;
  * the three session-projection keys `contextTimeline` / `contextHeaders` /
    `contextActivity` with their persisted state versions 29 / 1 / 6, and the
    wire payload shapes the browser half reads;
  * the five host routes `/api/dsh-cost-breakdown/{detail,backfill,balance,
    credits,skills}` and their POST / no-store / `{ok,value}` envelopes;
  * the slot registrations (conversation view, composer dock, assistant actions,
    input overlay, sidebar tab, Insights panel, plugins config card) and the
    settings schema field names, so persisted preferences keep working.

What is new, and differs from the earlier fork by design:

  * the architecture: wire / core / host / client layers, with the shared pure
    maths extracted into `src/core` and the HTTP channels split from the fold;
  * the fold engine: a draft-based reducer with per-event handlers instead of one
    monolithic switch, the same reference-discipline and all-or-nothing rules;
  * the browser half: a new data layer (price book, timeline reconciliation,
    cross-session aggregation) and new components with `cb-` prefixed styles;
  * the test suite: the earlier 142 spec files were removed and replaced by a
    new suite covering the same behaviour through the new modules.

Changes to the product relative to upstream dsh-context are documented in
README.md ("本仓库叠加的功能" in the earlier fork history). In short: the official
CNY price table with peak/off-peak windows and a Chinese public-holiday calendar,
per-platform spend in each platform's own unit, the composer-dock readout, and a
strict separation between token surfaces and money surfaces.

